{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q85806080","formula":"C₂₃H₃₄O₂","hill":"C23H34O2","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":23.0,"H":34.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"Tetrahydrocannabiphorol"},"descriptions":{"en":"Tetrahydrocannabiphorol (THCP) is a potent phytocannabinoid, a CB1 and CB2 receptor agonist which was known as a synthetic homologue of tetrahydrocannabinol (THC), but for the first time in 2019 was isolated as a trace natural product from Cannabis sativa. THCP is structurally similar to Δ9-THC, the main active component of cannabis, but with the pentyl side chain extended to heptyl. Since it has a longer side chain, its cannabinoid effects are \"far higher than Δ9-THC itself.\" Tetrahydrocannabiphorol has a reported binding affinity of 1.2 nM at CB1, approximately 33 times that of Δ9-THC (40 nM at CB1), however this does not mean it's 33x stronger per milligram."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":6453074,"mass":342.5,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCCCCCCC1=CC(=C2[C@@H]3C=C(CC[C@H]3C(OC2=C1)(C)C)C)O","inchikey":"OJTMRZHYTZMJKX-RTBURBONSA-N","iupac":"(6aR,10aR)-3-heptyl-6,6,9-trimethyl-6a,7,8,10a-tetrahydrobenzo[c]chromen-1-ol","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"6453074","atoms":59,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.382,"y":-1.979,"z":0.563,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.198,"y":2.694,"z":-0.816,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.562,"y":-0.951,"z":0.112,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.905,"y":0.293,"z":-0.535,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.661,"y":-2.196,"z":-0.071,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.999,"y":-1.085,"z":-0.409,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.47,"y":0.396,"z":-0.052,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.836,"y":0.128,"z":0.011,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.779,"y":1.512,"z":-0.319,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.1,"y":1.442,"z":-0.069,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.814,"y":-0.738,"z":0.453,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.325,"y":-2.417,"z":-1.556,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.257,"y":-3.507,"z":0.466,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.729,